    "event": null,
    "id": "whats-on/halloween-film-music-concert",
    "payload": {
      "description": "Prepare to be spellbound as the Docklands Sinfonia take you on a spine-tingling journey this Halloween. From haunting classics to magical adventures and supernatural favourites, the programme celebrates the mysterious, the macabre, and the wonderfully whimsical. This 75-minute concert features some of the most recognisable and powerful film scores – some of which were filmed on-site here, at the UK’s No. 1 heritage filming location. So, sit back, embrace the Halloween spirit, and enjoy an unforgettable evening of music that is sure to delight, surprise, and send a shiver down your spine. Age Recommendation: 5+ Programme (subject to change) Toccata and Fugue in D Minor Hocus Pocus Psycho: Intro Credits and Shower Scene Jaws Harry Potter Dark Knight Davy Jones (Pirates of the Caribbean) The Mummy Night on Bald Mountain Charlie and the Chocolate Factory Edward Scissor Hands Addams Family Scooby Doo Beetlejuice Nightmare Before Christmas Ghostbusters About Docklands Sinfonia Docklands Sinfonia is a diverse, dynamic and versatile orchestra working with composers, producers and promoters across film, rock, pop and classic music. A major cultural force in Docklands and beyond – the orchestra brings high-quality music to the area, staging ground-breaking concerts and creating a lasting legacy by inspiring generations of young people. Since its formation in 2009, Docklands Sinfonia has enjoyed incredible success with performances for Queen Elizabeth II at Buckingham Palace and with Grammy-award winner Imogen Heap at the Royal Albert Hall. The orchestra received standing ovations for its world premiere performances of Roy Budd’s score to the 1925 silent film, Phantom of the Opera at the Barbican and London Coliseum. It has appeared on BBC Radio 3 and BBC1 and performed the first-ever concerts in the Tower Bridge’s Bascule Chamber under the Thames. About the Chapel of St Peter & St Paul The concert takes place in the beautiful Chapel of St Peter & St Paul, part of Sir Christopher Wren’s original design for the Royal Hospital for Seamen at Greenwich. After a devastating fire, the Chapel was rebuilt in 1779 by James ‘Athenian’ Stuart. With its richly decorated ceiling, naval themes, and exceptional altarpiece painted by ‘the Raphael of America’, Benjamin West, the Chapel is now regarded as one of the finest intact neo-classical interiors in existence. Find out more Event T&Cs Tickets are non-refundable once purchased and cannot be exchanged. By attending this event, you acknowledge that photography and filming may take place for promotional and archival purposes. If you do not wish to be photographed or filmed, please inform a member of staff upon arrival. We reserve the right to refuse service to anyone that does not respect our site, staff, or other visitors. For full T&Cs please check our website here. Food is not permitted inside the Chapel. Only bottled water is permitted inside the Chapel.",
      "image_url": "https://et38c4vicjh.exactdn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/ORNC_Chapel-Concert_Credit-Docklands-Sinfonia_1-640x640.jpg?strip=all&quality=90&webp=90&avif=80",
      "label": "After Hours",
      "listed_on": "2026-09-26",
      "page_title": "Halloween Film Music LIVE! - Old Royal Naval College",
      "path": "/whats-on/halloween-film-music-concert/",
      "price_text": "Tickets: £35 (Adults), £10 (Child), £68-£75 (Family)",
      "title": "Halloween Film Music LIVE!",
      "url": "https://ornc.org/whats-on/halloween-film-music-concert/",
      "when": "Sat 31 Oct | 6.30pm-7.45pm"
    }
  },
  {
    "event": null,
    "id": "whats-on/murder-mystery-halloween-edition",
    "payload": {
      "description": "A haunting Halloween murder mystery in Admiral’s House. Step into a world of shadows, secrets, and suspense this Halloween, with a thrilling, after-hours murder mystery experience, set within the historic walls of Admiral’s House. As darkness falls, assemble your team of detectives to explore our historic buildings under the cover of night. You’ll need to hunt for hidden clues and interrogate enigmatic, spine-chilling suspects to piece together the puzzle before the witching hour. With 90 minutes to investigate, interrogate, and deduce, will your team crack the case, or will the culprit slip away into the night? Please note: Recommended age 16 and above. About the venue Admiral’s House is the oldest building of the Old Royal Naval College site, originally commissioned by King Charles II to be his King’s House in 1660. In 1745 the rooms became the official residence of the Governor of Greenwich Hospital. It then became known as Admiral’s House, as the Governor was almost always an Admiral.",
      "image_url": "https://et38c4vicjh.exactdn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/PAINTED_HALL_MURDER_MYSTERY-05555-640x640.jpg?strip=all&quality=90&webp=90&avif=80",
      "label": "After Hours",
      "listed_on": "2026-09-26",
      "page_title": "Murder Mystery Halloween Edition - Old Royal Naval College",
      "path": "/whats-on/murder-mystery-halloween-edition/",
      "price_text": "Tickets: £30 (Adults), £27 (Concession)",
      "title": "Murder Mystery Halloween Edition",
      "url": "https://ornc.org/whats-on/murder-mystery-halloween-edition/",
      "when": "Sat 31 Oct | 7pm-10pm"
    }
  },
